\title{Brute force algorithms}
\date{2026-08-26T09:43:32Z}
\tag{algorithms}
\tag{draft}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{Introduced via another [POGIL activity](https://hendrix-cs.github.io/csci382/pub/brute-force.pdf).  Some key takeaways:

\ul{
  \li{In this class we will consider solving problems with specified inputs and outputs.}
  \li{A \em{brute-force} algorithm is one that simply lists all possible outputs for the given inputs and checks which one has the desired properties.}
  \li{This semester we will consider a lot of clever ways to solve problems faster than brute force.  But that's not always possible.}
}

}
